<p> </p>

<p> When should cellulitis improve? </p>

<ul>
	<li>Expect symptomatic improvement in 24-48 hrs, visible arrest of spread after 48-72 hrs, and closer to 72 hrs for defervescence and improved leukocytosis</li>
	<li>In the outpatient setting, repeat evaluation in 48 hrs to monitor clinical response </li>
	<li>Not improving as expected? Consider resistant organisms, deeper infection, or organism not covered by current antibiotic regimen</li>
</ul>

